<article class="env-definition" id="006K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/006K">Definition <span data-tag="006K">6.4.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>presheaf of abelian groups on $X$</em> or an <em>abelian presheaf over $X$</em> is a presheaf of sets $\mathcal{F}$ such that for each open $U \subset X$ the set $\mathcal{F}(U)$ is endowed with the structure of an abelian group, and such that all restriction maps $\rho ^ U_ V$ are homomorphisms of abelian groups, see Lemma <a href="/tag/006J" data-tag="006J">6.4.3</a> above. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>morphism of abelian presheaves over $X$</em> $\varphi : \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G}$ is a morphism of presheaves of sets which induces a homomorphism of abelian groups $\mathcal{F}(U) \to \mathcal{G}(U)$ for every open $U \subset X$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The category of presheaves of abelian groups on $X$ is denoted $\textit{PAb}(X)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>